    "detailedExplanationEn": "🎯 Correct Answer: Option D (\"Obsolescence threats weighing on combustion engine subcontracting jobs\")\n\n• Textual Evidence (Report on  transition industrielle):\nIn response to \"Direct industrial consequence of transitioning to electric vehicles:\", the passage states: \"INDUSTRIAL ECONOMICS — MANUFACTURING TRANSITION REVIEW: RECONVERTING AUTOMOTIVE SUPPLY CHAINS.\n\nThe forced automotive transition from internal combustion engines to electric vehicles deeply disrupts industrial regions specialized in mechanical subcontracting. Manufacturing electric motors requires significantly fewer complex parts, directly threatening thousands of machining and foundry jobs.\n\nAverting severe labor crises, public authorities and manufacturers must fund massive worker retraining programs toward emerging sectors like battery manufacturing and rare metal recycling.\".\nOption D (\"Obsolescence threats weighing on combustion engine subcontracting jobs\") accurately conveys the essential information presented in the text.\n\n• Detailed Distractor Breakdown (Incorrect Options):\n  - Option A (\"Surge in the number of complex mechanical engine parts manufactured\") [INCORRECT - NUMERICAL OR TEMPORAL DISTRACTOR TRAP]: Uses inaccurate numerical or temporal anchors (\"Surge in the number of complex mechanical engine parts manufactured\") that distort explicit passage figures.\n  - Option B (\"Permanent closure of all national highways and interstate road systems\") [INCORRECT - DIRECT CONTRADICTION TRAP]: Claims the exact opposite of the passage's findings (\"Permanent closure of all national highways and interstate road systems\"), representing a direct contradiction.\n  - Option C (\"Mandatory requirements to build passenger cars running on charcoal\") [INCORRECT - NUMERICAL OR TEMPORAL DISTRACTOR TRAP]: Uses inaccurate numerical or temporal anchors (\"Mandatory requirements to build passenger cars running on charcoal\") that distort explicit passage figures.\n  - Option D (\"Obsolescence threats weighing on combustion engine subcontracting jobs\") [CORRECT]: Accurately conveys the passage's verified meaning without distortion."
