    "detailedExplanationEn": "🎯 Correct Answer: Option D (\"Preserving traditional heirloom local fruit tree varieties\")\n\n• Textual Evidence (Article on  biodiversité végétale):\nIn response to \"Essential role of conservatory orchards planted by the municipal council:\", the passage states: \"URBAN BOTANY — CIVIC FLORA BULLETIN: PRESERVING MUNICIPAL CONSERVATORY ORCHARDS.\n\nPreventing the extinction of heirloom fruit tree varieties (local apples, pears, plums), city parks established two conservatory orchards on the city outskirts. Open access, these orchards host over 80 traditional varieties adapted to regional climates.\n\nCitizens participate in pruning, grafting, and autumn fruit harvests, discovering historical fruit flavors.\".\nOption D (\"Preserving traditional heirloom local fruit tree varieties\") accurately conveys the essential information presented in the text.\n\n• Detailed Distractor Breakdown (Incorrect Options):\n  - Option A (\"Selling exotic tropical fruit imported via air freight\") [INCORRECT - LEXICAL LURE & UNSTATED ASSUMPTION TRAP]: Reuses passage keywords (\"Selling exotic tropical fruit imported via air freight\") while introducing an unstated assumption or off-topic conclusion.\n  - Option B (\"Prohibiting citizens from consuming fresh fruit produce\") [INCORRECT - LEXICAL LURE & UNSTATED ASSUMPTION TRAP]: Reuses passage keywords (\"Prohibiting citizens from consuming fresh fruit produce\") while introducing an unstated assumption or off-topic conclusion.\n  - Option C (\"Replacing fruit trees with asphalt vehicle parking spaces\") [INCORRECT - LEXICAL LURE & UNSTATED ASSUMPTION TRAP]: Reuses passage keywords (\"Replacing fruit trees with asphalt vehicle parking spaces\") while introducing an unstated assumption or off-topic conclusion.\n  - Option D (\"Preserving traditional heirloom local fruit tree varieties\") [CORRECT]: Accurately conveys the passage's verified meaning without distortion."
