    "detailedExplanationEn": "🎯 Correct Answer: Option C (\"Creating new homes without sealing new ground via urban sprawl\")\n\n• Textual Evidence (Analysis of  sobriété foncière):\nIn response to \"Advantage of adding timber rooftop extensions to existing downtown buildings:\", the passage states: \"URBAN PLANNING — LIVING ENVIRONMENT REVIEW: GENTLE DENSITY AND BUILDING ROOFTOP EXTENSIONS.\n\nCreating affordable downtown housing without destroying urban parks or encroaching on rural farmland, architects favor 'gentle densification'. This strategy adds 2 to 3 timber-framed stories atop existing buildings.\n\nThis rapid building method preserves ground footprints while funding overall energy retrofits for original buildings through sales of new rooftop units.\".\nOption C (\"Creating new homes without sealing new ground via urban sprawl\") accurately conveys the essential information presented in the text.\n\n• Detailed Distractor Breakdown (Incorrect Options):\n  - Option A (\"Demolishing old buildings to construct concrete towers\") [INCORRECT - NUMERICAL OR TEMPORAL DISTRACTOR TRAP]: Uses inaccurate numerical or temporal anchors (\"Demolishing old buildings to construct concrete towers\") that distort explicit passage figures.\n  - Option B (\"Forcing top-floor residents to relocate permanently\") [INCORRECT - LEXICAL LURE & UNSTATED ASSUMPTION TRAP]: Reuses passage keywords (\"Forcing top-floor residents to relocate permanently\") while introducing an unstated assumption or off-topic conclusion.\n  - Option C (\"Creating new homes without sealing new ground via urban sprawl\") [CORRECT]: Accurately conveys the passage's verified meaning without distortion.\n  - Option D (\"Increasing heating bills for all building tenants\") [INCORRECT - LEXICAL LURE & UNSTATED ASSUMPTION TRAP]: Reuses passage keywords (\"Increasing heating bills for all building tenants\") while introducing an unstated assumption or off-topic conclusion."
